      "problem": "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\frac{7}{10}$ is a rational number\n\nII. $-\\frac{5}{3}$ is a rational number\n\nIII. $3$ is a rational number",
      "worked_solution": "A rational number is any number that can be written as the ratio of two integers.\n\nNow, let's go through each number in turn.\n\n- $\\frac{7}{10}$ is a rational number.\n\n- $-\\frac{5}{3}$ is a rational number. It can be written as $\\frac{(-5)}{3}.$\n\n- $3$ is a rational number. It can be written as $\\frac{3}{1}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"",
